  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a strong, consistent relationship between K-252a and BOKU, mediated through a common target molecule. The target molecule, [(3S,9S,12R,13R,14R,15R)-13-hydroxy-6-(1-hydroxyethyl)-12,14-dimethyl-2,5,8,11-tetraoxo-9-(propan-2-yl)-15-tridecyl-1-oxa-4,7,10-triazacyclopentadecan-3-yl]methyl acetate, is identified as the target of K-252a in three distinct paths, with varying scores. This molecule is also the target of leukemia cells and solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which are both targets of K-252a. The shared target molecule appears to be a critical mediator of K-252a's effect, as it is linked to BOKU in multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that K-252a may act by modulating the activity of this transporter, which in turn influences BOKU. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a single, consistent target molecule across different pathways, indicating a potential direct or indirect interaction between K-252a and BOKU through this molecular bridge.",
